<http://data.europa.eu/a4g/resource/8b83518c-4346-4d7b-a551-ff21e1eb62c6-01/SelectionCriterion$_PriorInformationNotice1_ProcurementProjectLot1_TenderingTerms1_UBLExtensions1_UBLExtension1_ExtensionContent1_EformsExtension1_SelectionCriteria1>
  a epo:SelectionCriterion;
  epo:hasSelectionCriterionType <http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/selection-criterion/sui-act>;
  epo:isUsedForCandidateRestriction false;
  dct:description """Ability to perform professional activity
The right to participate in the procedure has every economic operator who is registered as a physical or legal entity for the performance of the activity related to the subject of procurement or belongs to an appropriate professional association in accordance with the regulations of the country where it is registered.
The right to participate in the procedure has every economic operator who fulfills the special conditions for carrying out the activity prescribed in accordance with the law, which refers to the subject of procurement.
To prove the ability to perform a professional activity, the economic operator should submit:
 Certificate of registered activity as proof that he is registered as a physical or legal entity for the performance of the activity related to the object of procurement or proof that he belongs to an appropriate professional association in accordance with the regulations of the country where he is registered.
 License \"A\" for performance in accordance with the Building Law, issued by a competent authority
 Certified trainer for PP fire system
The economic operator proves the fulfillment of the minimum conditions from subsection 5.3.3.1 by submitting:
a) list of performed services in the last three years, with values, dates, buyers (contracting authorities or economic operators), providing a certificate for performed services.
b) description of the technical staff and technical authorities that will participate in the execution of the public procurement, especially those responsible for quality control
"""@en;
  skos:prefLabel "Ability to perform professional activity"@en .

